WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:24.750
In order to restore Mokuba's memories, Kaiba used Blue-Eyes for a final showdown.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:29.950
But Noa trampled Kaiba's hopes and turned them into stone.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:33.060
Noa, I can't forgive you!

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:38.040
I'll carry on Kaiba's duelist pride and his feelings for Mokuba!

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.310
Let's battle, Noa!

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:44.020
If you want to claim to be the true winner, defeat me first!

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:50.020
Inherited Deck
Yugi vs Noa

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:05.940
Since you modified your deck, I'll build a new deck too.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:12.970
Yugi, you play a strategic deck.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:16.910
But Seto plays a power deck that summons strong monsters.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:19.650
Your decks aren't compatible.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:24.160
You now have cards that don't fit your strategy, so you're at a disadvantage.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.690
What's that light?

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:33.170
With Shinato's arrival, his Ark's effects are gone.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.200
The cards in the Ark return to the graveyard.

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:42.210
Even if the Ark's effects are gone, Yugi has no monsters on his field or cards in his hand.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:46.210
Noa is now the Deck Master, and he has 3300 attack points.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:52.000
If Yugi doesn't draw a monster card, he'll lose!

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:52.720
Yugi!

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.890
Yugi, it's your turn.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:05.460
Don't tell me you're scared?

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:08.930
If you want, I'll let you change your Deck Master.

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:10.470
I don't need to!

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:15.580
I can sense Kaiba and Mokuba's hearts in this deck.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:16.580
Here I go!

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:20.200
Kaiba and Mokuba, let's make a comeback together!

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.950
My turn!  I draw!

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:28.180
I summon Gazelle the King of Mythical Beasts in defense position!

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:31.460
Nice!  He managed to draw a monster!

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:34.460
You're so lucky.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:37.460
Actually, you don't know when to give up.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:45.050
Even if you summon a monster card, this duel is over if I draw a monster.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:46.470
My turn!

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.450
Too bad.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:54.260
I can tell that you can't defeat me yet.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:57.480
But I still have the advantage.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.910
Shinato, King of a Higher Plane attacks!

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.920
Six Realms of Transmigration!

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:23.480
No way!  My monster was in defense position!

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.740
Why did I lose life points?  Can it be?

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.170
Exactly.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:30.570
Shinato's effect already activated.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:35.290
When Shinato destroys your defending monster, your life points are halved.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:45.300
Shinato's Deck Master ability also gives me life points equal to the damage you took.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:48.520
That Deck Master isn't fair!

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:51.300
Damn!  This duel is hopeless!

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:57.800
Yugi, I don't understand why you took over this impossible duel.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:01.680
I thought you and Seto were enemies.

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.510
Yes.  Kaiba and I are rivals.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:10.320
History may have destined for us to become enemies.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:16.640
But there's one thing we both won't harm.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.330
What is it?

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.830
It's the bond among duelists!

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:22.920
Bond?

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.840
What a lame answer.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:32.800
While you used Mokuba and tried every trick in the book, Kaiba fought fair and square.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:38.180
By holding on to that pride, duelists are connected by a strong bond!

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.930
And I'll carry on that bond!

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:42.850
And defeat you!

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.320
My turn!

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:50.440
I set a monster in defense position.

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:51.630
I end my turn.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:54.960
You drew another monster card.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:59.080
But how long can you survive by relying on luck?

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.860
My turn!

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:03.830
Too bad, Yugi.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:06.140
This will be your last turn.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:11.050
As a parting gift, I'll show you the true nature of my deck.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:16.600
I summon my Spirit Monster, Yata-Garasu, in attack position.

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:21.560
Spirit Monster?

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:22.830
Here I go!

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:25.560
Shinato, King of a Higher Plane attacks!

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.260
Six Realms of Transmigration!

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.710
What's with that Guardian?

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:42.040
Monsters with at least 1900 attack points can't destroy Obnoxious Celtic Guard, Noa!

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.300
So annoying!

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:49.720
I activate the spell card, Spring of Rebirth, from my hand!

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:56.360
Every time a card on the field returns to the hand, Spring of Rebirth restores 500 life points.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:58.550
Return, Yata-Garasu!

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:05.640
Spring of Rebirth now activates.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:11.480
I regain 500 life points.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:15.920
Why did his monster return to his hand?

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:20.920
I see.  Yata-Garasu is a part of the Spirit series.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.940
That's right.

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:30.430
Pegasus of Industrial Illusions created this rare series based on Asian mythology.

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:36.230
All Spirit Monsters have a certain effect as its main feature.

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:40.110
Spirit Monsters cannot be Special Summoned.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:43.870
When they're summoned, they return to the hand during that End Phase.

00:07:43.870 --> 00:07:47.480
I see!  Spring of Rebirth forms a combo!

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:51.080
Even without Shinato's Ark's life restoration effect...

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:54.990
...he regains life points every time he plays a Spirit Card.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.990
I end my turn.

00:07:58.480 --> 00:07:59.800
My turn!

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:03.130
This is Kaiba's...

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:09.870
He combined with his Deck Master and is out on the field.

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:14.360
Kaiba, I may be able to defeat him with your card.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:16.870
I set a monster in defense position!

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:19.880
I end my turn.

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.320
My turn.  I draw!

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:26.360
I summon my Spirit Monster, Asura Priest.

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:35.040
Asura Priest, attack Obnoxious Celtic Guard!

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.220
Thousand Knives of Hell!

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:49.400
Obnoxious Celtic Guard's effect activates against monsters with at least 1900 attack points.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:54.640
Asura Priest has 1700 attack points, so that effect doesn't activate.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:56.180
Vanish!

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:02.140
Asura Priest's effect activates!

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:05.220
What?

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.460
He finished attacking, but he has knives again!

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:15.460
Asura Priest's effect allows him to attack all of your monsters.

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:20.250
If he destroys your defending monster, you'll be defenseless.

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.470
I'll finish you with my own hands.

00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:25.940
You should never have opposed me.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:27.220
Go!  Asura Priest!

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:29.210
Thousand Knives of Hell!

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:32.350
Vanish!

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:34.850
Caught you, Noa.

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:40.340
The card you attacked belongs to Kaiba.

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:44.050
Cyber Jar!

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:49.370
Cyber Jar destroys all monsters on the field.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:52.450
All monsters on the field...

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:57.870
Since you combined with your Deck Master, that includes you, Noa!

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:07.960
Incredible, Yugi!

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.550
What a comeback!

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:11.540
Yugi wins!

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:12.550
All right!

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:22.210
I activate my Deck Master's last ability!

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:23.430
Reincarnation!

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:32.600
He disappeared.

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:34.700
Did Yugi win?

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:43.040
No way!  He survived!

00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:48.720
Cyber Jar didn't work?

00:10:48.720 --> 00:10:51.360
I was careless, Yugi.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:56.000
I never thought I'd have to use my Deck Master's last ability.

00:10:56.310 --> 00:11:00.200
When my Deck Master is about to be destroyed...

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:07.660
...Reincarnation negates that effect and returns my Deck Master to his original position.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:12.710
Once I use this ability, Shinato can no longer be summoned to the field.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:16.880
Noa, Cyber Jar's effect is still active.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:20.660
We both draw five cards from our decks.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:25.090
If we draw any monster cards, we can Special Summon them in any position.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:30.930
I Special Summon Sangan and Gamma The Magnet Warrior in defense position!

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:35.040
Noa!  Summon your monster cards!

00:11:35.680 --> 00:11:36.940
Yugi!

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:39.070
What's wrong with Noa?

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:40.540
But you can't.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:44.850
Spirit Monsters can't be Special Summoned!

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:47.950
Here I go!  My turn!

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:52.510
I tribute Gamma The Magnet Warrior and Sangan!

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:56.460
Sangan's effect activates.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:12:01.960
I add a monster with 1500-or-fewer attack points from my deck to my hand.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:05.330
I add Big Shield Gardna to my hand.

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:08.200
The monster I'll summon is...

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:12.710
Come out!  Dark Magician!

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.710
Dark Magician?

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:18.710
Noa!  Your field is empty!

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:21.460
Here I go!  Dark Magician!

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:23.520
Attack him directly!

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:24.990
Black Magic!

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:30.220
Nice, Yugi!

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:34.500
It's the perfect strategy against Noa's Spirit Monster Deck!

00:12:34.840 --> 00:12:36.660
Do your best, Yugi!

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:38.000
Keep it up!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.500
Yugi...

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:43.200
What's wrong, Noa?

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:45.510
The battle is only getting started!

00:13:03.560 --> 00:13:07.800
Yugi!  How dare you humiliate me!

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:09.730
Humiliate you?

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:15.470
It's nothing compared to what you and Gozaburo did to Kaiba and Mokuba!

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:18.860
I created this world!

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:23.730
You're not allowed to hurt the creator!

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:27.300
I've never heard of a creator who uses others as stepping stones.

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:31.320
Noa!  Ever soul has a home!

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.220
Every soul has a home...

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:40.090
That steel casket isn't your soul's home!

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:45.600
Noa, I'll free your soul in this duel!

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:46.800
Silence, Yugi!

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.600
You're the one who'll vanish!

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:49.910
My turn.

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:53.520
I activate the spell card, Next World!

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:03.580
Dark Magician?

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:10.540
This spell card absorbs the energy of the monster drawn on the mandala of hell.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:15.100
And I can summon a monster with the same Level from my hand.

00:14:15.320 --> 00:14:20.600
I summon the Spirit Monster, Yamata Dragon!

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:27.610
What?

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:29.610
What's that?

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:33.200
2600 attack points!

00:14:37.450 --> 00:14:39.950
Take this!  Corpses and Blood!

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:51.510
Dark Magician!

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:56.910
My Deck Master's ability activates.

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:59.070
Come back, Yamata Dragon!

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:06.800
Since my monster returns to my hand, Spring of Rebirth's effect activates.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:10.600
I gain 500 life points.

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:17.280
Since Shinato is gone, my life points won't be halved.

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:19.090
But the damage I dealt is...

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:24.620
Yugi, you only have 100 life points left.

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:26.500
There's nothing you can do.

00:15:27.660 --> 00:15:29.060
You're fine!

00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:31.260
Yugi!  Trust yourself!

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:32.870
Anzu!

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:35.610
Yugi!  This is when you have to be strong!

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:37.550
Jonouchi...

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:46.370
If I even have a 1% chance to win, I'll believe in my deck!

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:47.660
My turn!

00:15:48.370 --> 00:15:52.660
I activate the spell card, Swords of Revealing Light, from my hand!

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.200
He doesn't give up!

00:16:02.200 --> 00:16:03.540
Nice!

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:05.550
This will buy you time!

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:08.820
Yugi!  Do your best!

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:12.740
Swords of Revealing Light won't let him attack for three turns!

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:15.240
Use this time to find a way to counterattack!

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:19.720
Can it be that they're keeping his spirit strong?

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:23.090
I summon Kuriboh!

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:29.960
Kuriboh, attack Noa directly!

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:40.320
Did something touch me?

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:44.600
What a pathetic attack.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:49.570
Fine.  Go ahead and keep attacking me.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:55.500
But when Swords of Revealing Light wears off, I predict that I'll instantly end you.

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:02.600
My predictions have never been wrong in this duel.

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:04.000
My turn!

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:08.000
I set a monster card in defense position.

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:10.500
I end my turn.

00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:14.510
Swords of Revealing Light's first turn has ended.

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:16.500
My turn!

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:19.010
Dark Magician Girl.

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:25.020
The ability of my Deck Master, Kaiser Sea Horse, only affects Light Attribute monsters.

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:28.950
I can't use my Deck Master's ability to summon Dark Magician Girl.

00:17:29.350 --> 00:17:32.460
I have to get monsters on my field for now.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:36.700
Big Shield Gardna in defense position!

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:40.400
And I switch Kuriboh to defense position!

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:42.850
I end my turn.

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:44.510
My turn!

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:48.270
I summon a monster in defense position.

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:53.780
And I set a card and end my turn.

00:17:54.160 --> 00:17:57.820
Swords of Revealing Light's second turn has ended.

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.490
My turn!

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:02.990
I don't have a card in my hand that can make a comeback.

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:05.990
I set a card.

00:18:05.990 --> 00:18:07.490
I end my turn.

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:11.530
Seems you can't get a card to turn things around.

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:14.960
My prediction will soon come true.

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:16.500
Prepare yourself.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:19.240
Hang in there, Yugi!

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:21.400
Yugi will win!

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:22.660
That's right!

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:24.240
We believe in you!

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:29.080
It's foolish to believe when there's no evidence that he'll win.

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:31.370
We don't need evidence!

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:37.280
A lonely guy like you with no friends can never understand!

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:41.390
Our bond can make the impossible possible!

00:18:41.740 --> 00:18:43.030
Everyone...

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:48.400
Just like Kaiba has Mokuba, Yugi has you.

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:50.400
I can't allow that.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:54.910
I'll test how strong your bond is!

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:00.420
Otogi!

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:04.130
Otogi!

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.660
How's that!

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:13.040
When Yugi loses, you'll all end up the same.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:16.630
He's lucky he didn't have to feel this fear.

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:19.630
You're out of control!

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:28.060
When Yugi runs out of life points, you'll regret trusting this foolish duelist.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:33.620
And while you're regretting, I'll turn you into stone, like Seto and Mokuba.

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:40.650
And standing at the center of all this resentment will be you, Yugi.

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:44.660
They will be glaring at you for eternity!

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:47.160
What's so funny?

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.500
Pathetic.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:54.000
You haven't matured since your accident!

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:55.670
You're still childish!

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:57.740
What?

00:19:57.740 --> 00:19:59.960
Look at them!

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:04.080
Yugi!  We believe in you!

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:07.410
Your threats don't scare us!

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:10.150
What's with that look in their eyes?

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:13.640
Noa!  Remember that look!

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:16.150
Those eyes believe in our bond!

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:22.310
As you wish, I'll send you all to hell!

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:23.550
My turn!

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:26.090
I activate my trap card!

00:20:26.090 --> 00:20:27.530
Pyro Clock of Destiny!

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:35.360
What?  Swords of Revealing Light is gone!

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:40.450
Pyro Clock of Destiny moves the turn count forward by one.

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:43.750
Your protection is gone.

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.480
I summon a monster in attack position!

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:48.320
Come out, Otohime!

00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:51.540
Otohime's effect activates.

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:57.330
When Otohime is summoned, one of your monsters switches battle positions.

00:20:57.640 --> 00:20:59.560
I choose...

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:01.430
Kuriboh!

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:07.440
Oh no!  Kuriboh is in attack position!

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:11.340
I tribute Otohime and another monster.

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:14.850
Come out, Yamata Dragon!

00:21:21.650 --> 00:21:24.000
It's over now!

00:21:24.000 --> 00:21:25.980
Yamata Dragon attacks!

00:21:29.190 --> 00:21:31.530
Vanish, Yugi!

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:49.860
Yugi struggles to survive against Noa's powerful monster attacks.

00:21:49.860 --> 00:21:57.460
Noa uses his Deck Master's ability and life restoration combo to get over 10,000 life points.

00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:02.860
And every time it's Noa's turn, one of us gets turned into stone.

00:22:02.860 --> 00:22:07.700
But we still believe that Yugi will win!

00:22:07.700 --> 00:22:11.200
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
10000 Life Points vs 100!!

00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:12.760
Duel, standby!

00:22:16.520 --> 00:22:24.420
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:24.420 --> 00:22:33.370
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:38.340
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:38.340 --> 00:22:42.310
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:42.740 --> 00:22:50.280
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:50.280 --> 00:22:53.850
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:53.850 --> 00:22:58.620
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:22:58.620 --> 00:23:08.730
And walk it without stopping

00:23:08.730 --> 00:23:16.340
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:16.570 --> 00:23:25.310
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:25.310 --> 00:23:33.290
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:43.130
I hide it in my heart...
Secret Paradise
